# Copy to .env.local.
# Dev database: `pnpm db:up` (Postgres 18 in Docker on 127.0.0.1:5433). The
# scripts and the app default to that exact URL, so DATABASE_URL is optional in
# dev — set it only to point somewhere else.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=           # openssl rand -hex 32
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:37264
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5433/postgres
# Prod (Neon) + OAuth — leave unset in dev:
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://...neon...
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Salts the hash behind the public like cap's visitor key.
# `app/lib/likes-cap.ts` THROWS when this is unset and NODE_ENV=production, rather
# than falling back to its dev default: this repo is public, so the default salt is a
# published one, and `like_grants.visitor_key` would be a reversible IP hash (2^32
# IPv4 enumeration) while the schema comment claims otherwise. Any long random value:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# LIKES_SALT=

# OPTIONAL. Canonical origin for canonical links, og:image URLs, sitemap.xml and
# robots.txt. `app/lib/site.ts` defaults to https://frames.zentry.com, so set this
# only when serving the explorer somewhere else (a staging domain you actually
# want indexed, a fork). Deliberately NOT derived from BETTER_AUTH_URL — that is
# the auth callback origin, which in dev is localhost, and letting it win here
# would publish localhost canonicals from any build that saw a dev .env.
# Preview deployments need no value: they canonicalise to production on purpose
# and robots.txt disallows them wholesale.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://frames.zentry.com

# SET IN PRODUCTION. Google Search Console ownership token, served as
# <meta name="google-site-verification"> on every page. Get it from Search
# Console → Add property → HTML tag. No default on purpose: the token belongs to
# whoever owns the property, so a value in this public repo would be one every
# fork also served. Unset omits the tag entirely, which is correct — an empty
# `content` fails the check.
# FOOTGUN: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time, so changing this in Vercel
# takes effect on the next deploy, not on a restart.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# SET IN PRODUCTION. Contact email stamped into the User-Agent the official-data
# proxy (/api/zframes-proxy) sends upstream. SEC's fair-access policy asks for a
# declared, contactable UA; without this the relay falls back to a generic
# browser UA — datacenter IPs claiming to be desktop Chrome is exactly the
# traffic SEC blocks by IP at volume.
# ZFRAMES_CONTACT=hello@zentry.com
